===Noun===
{{en-noun|?}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The second [[cervical vertebra]] of the [[spine]] which forms the pivot upon which the first cervical vertebra (the [[atlas]]), which carries the head, rotates.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1914| author=| title=Human Anatomy: A Complete Systematic Treatise|page=215| passage=The union of the atlas and '''epistropheus''' is described in this section because (1) there is often a direct communication between the synovial cavity of the transverse epistropic and the occipito-atlantal joints; (2) the rotatory movements of the head take place around the dens (odontoid process); and (3) important ligaments from the dens pass over the atlas to the occiput.}}

